# KBI Capstone Project — Music Genre Classification

## Overview

Python ML/AI capstone that classifies music genres using the GTZAN dataset. Current model: SVM (Support Vector Classifier) with StandardScaler + PCA preprocessing, trained on hand-crafted audio features (MFCCs, chroma, spectral features, tempo, etc.) via librosa.

Goal: compare classifiers from simple sklearn models up to deep neural networks (Keras) for this task.

## File Structure

- `./data/` — `features_3_sec.csv`, `features_30_sec.csv`, `test_songs/`, `images_original/`, `genres_original/`
- `./streamlit/` — `Classifier.py` (main app), `pages/1_Model_Stats.py`
- `./capstone_project.ipynb` — EDA, feature analysis, model experimentation
- `./music_genre_classifier.py` — Production `MusicGenreClassifier` (SVM pipeline)

## Current Model

`music_genre_classifier.py`: `StandardScaler → PCA (95% variance) → SVC (RBF, C=15)`. Features: chroma STFT, RMS, spectral centroid/bandwidth/rolloff, ZCR, harmonics, percussive, tempo, 20 MFCCs (mean + var). Trained on `features_3_sec.csv` by default; `use_30_sec=True` for 30s segments.

## Run the App

From project root:

```bash
streamlit run streamlit/Classifier.py
```

## Learning Goal

Compare classifiers for 10-class genre prediction (GTZAN: blues, classical, country, disco, hiphop, jazz, metal, pop, reggae, rock): baseline sklearn (KNN, DT, Naive Bayes, Logistic Regression, Random Forest, SVM), ensembles (Gradient Boosting, XGBoost), deep nets (Dense, CNN, RNN/LSTM) via Keras.
